sub:assertion {
  <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/claim/high-composite-with-failing-gates> a delphi:Claim ;
    rdfs:label "On the winged-zebrafish run the scorer's composite is 0.878 and 'plausible' while 2 of the 5 named gates fail and 2 cannot be assessed, and the validator withholds the word 'validated'."@en ;
    dct:description "STATUS: this is a single-run observation from one fixture (the winged-zebrafish run against base zebrafish-adult, desired phenotype: glides at least 5 m from a 1 m launch and survives 10-30 C as an adult), reported as recorded in swarm/benchmark/fixtures/gt-l4-t1.json#results. It is unsigned and unreplicated; no second run, second design or independent re-scoring stands behind it. What was recorded: phenotype_similarity passed, functional_resolution and physics_check failed, genotype_similarity and lean_check could not be assessed. The scorer's own composite on that same run, 0.878 flagged plausible, version 1.0.0, is in swarm/benchmark/fixtures/gt-l4-t1.json#composite_score_from_the_scorer; that fixture notes it is carried through for reference, is not the report's verdict, and has no gate feeding it, so the high composite and the failing gates are two separate readings placed side by side, not one computed from the other. The validator's reason for withholding the word 'validated' is quoted in swarm/benchmark/fixtures/gt-l4-t1.json#verdict.withheld_because: 2 gate(s) failed, 2 gate(s) could not be assessed, 3 biological scale(s) (cell, tissue, organ_system) could not be assessed, and no sequence was compared at any locus. The command-line exit code of 1 (any gate failed) follows the rule at sim-engine/validate-cli.mjs:17. WHAT THIS DOES NOT ESTABLISH: it does not show the winged-zebrafish design is biologically invalid, and it does not show it is valid; it does not show the composite 0.878 is wrong in general, only that it disagrees in wording with the gates on this one run; it does not show the gates themselves are correct, since a failing gate is the gate's output, not independent ground truth; it says nothing about any other design; no sequence was compared at any locus, and the cell, tissue and organ_system scales were not assessed, so the gap between the composite and the gates cannot be traced to biology from this record."@en ;
    delphi:hasEvidence <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/high-composite-with-failing-gates> .
}